OL,3,GNEWSATwo sentenced in #266m gold money
OL,4,Alaundering plot
OL,5,
OL,6,FTwo men have been sentenced for their
OL,7,Fpart in a #266m money-laundering plot
OL,8,Fbased out of a scrap jewellery
OL,9,Fbusiness.
OL,11,FBaqa Haider and Nathan Rivers played a
OL,12,Fpart in the "industrial scale"
OL,13,Foperation, which involved processing
OL,14,Fbags of cash to buy gold grain that was
OL,15,Fthen exported to Dubai with fake
OL,16,Finvoices, police said.
OL,18,FHaider, 51, was responsible for bogus
OL,19,Finvoices and exporting the gold while
OL,20,FRivers, 45, worked in the Fowler
OL,21,FOldfield jewellery site in Bradford.
OL,23,APub: 01-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBYrk Lincs NewsCReg TVFWeather
